The comparison of PPO and SAC reveals several patterns in training time, performance, and convergence. For all problems, SAC required a minimum of one order of magnitude fewer steps than PPO to obtain convergence. The SAC advantage in training time stands in stark contrast to SACs convergence difficulties. SAC was highly hyperparametersensitive compared to PPO, which resulted in additional time being spent to determine the


